sys/z8001/drv/ATTIC -- not built, not linked, not a source of truth.

Nothing here is compiled.  hostbuild/link-kernel.sh links exactly one disk
driver, ../wd.c; these are earlier or alternate revisions of it that came
across with the donor tree, kept as history only.

The partition table is the trap.  Each file carries its own hand-typed
wdbtab[], and the tables disagree with each other and with the machine.
The live table is generated into <wdbtab.h> by hostbuild/dist.py from
os/dist/media/*.media, and ../wd.c includes it.  For the real layout read
os/dist/media/*.media or the generated hostbuild/build/gen/wdbtab.h,
never a table in here.

wd.old		WD + Commodore floppy controller, April 12 1985; 20 MB table
wd.c.old	WD hard disk only, March 18 1985; the oldest copy here
wd8.c		alternate controller build, 10336-block partitions (20 MB)
wd8atasi.c	same, retabled for the Atasi 42 MB drive; 20944-block partitions
junkwd.c	January 29 1985, named "junk" by the donor; 5168-block partitions
